## 2. Binary Container Topology & 32-Byte O(1) Header (`UniHeader`) Every `.uni` v8.0 file begins with a fixed **32-byte AVX2-aligned header** encoded in
Little-Endian byte order (`<4sHHIIQ4s4s`). Network controllers (SmartNIC/eBPF) and optical
data-diode buffers validate this header in O(1) constant time prior to dynamic heap allocation.
```text
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| 0x00 - 0x03 (4B) | MAGIC_BYTES : ASCII "UNI8" (0x55 0x4E 0x49 0x38) |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| 0x04 - 0x05 (2B) | PROTO_FLAGS : Version (0x0800) & Mode Bitmask |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| 0x06 - 0x07 (2B) | NODE_BITMAP : 16-bit Active Node Presence Mask |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| 0x08 - 0x0B (4B) | PAYLOAD_LIMIT : Exact Payload Size in Bytes (uint32)|
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| 0x0C - 0x0F (4B) | SESSION_SALT : 32-bit Hardware TRNG Entropy Salt |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| 0x10 - 0x17 (8B) | TIMESTAMP_US : 64-bit Microsecond Epoch Counter |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| 0x18 - 0x1B (4B) | MERKLE_TAG : Truncated 32-bit Root Hash Anchor |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| 0x1C - 0x1F (4B) | HEADER_ECC : 32-bit Blake2s/CRC32 Header Check |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| 0x20 - End | Encrypted TLV Node Stream + Optional RS(255,223) |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
Header Field Definitions
MAGIC_BYTES (4B, char[4]): Constant "UNI8" ("UNIM" in dedicated medical hardware profiles).
Identifies the stream as a non-executable .uni container.
PROTO_FLAGS (2B, uint16): Protocol version and hardware integrity status bits (e.g., bit
0x0001 = Hardware Tamper-Mesh Intact; bit 0x0002 = Reed-Solomon FEC Appended).
NODE_BITMAP (2B, uint16): Bitmask indicating which node indices (0..15) are populated in the
payload.
PAYLOAD_LIMIT (4B, uint32): Exact byte length of the following node stream. Any packet
whose physical length mismatches PAYLOAD_LIMIT is dropped immediately at the hardware
boundary, neutralizing buffer-overflow and Payload Denial-of-State (DoS) attacks.
SESSION_SALT (4B, uint32): Random salt generated per session by a hardware True Random
Number Generator (TRNG) for HKDF key derivation.
TIMESTAMP_US (8B, uint64): 64-bit UTC microsecond counter, eliminating the Year-2038
overflow issue and preventing packet replay attacks.
MERKLE_TAG (4B, uint8[4]): First 4 bytes of the full 256-bit SHA-256 Merkle root covering all
nodes.
HEADER_ECC (4B, uint8[4]): 4-byte Blake2s-32 digest computed over bytes 0x00..0x1B,
verified in constant time. 3. Universal Node Types (UniNodeType Specification)
Following the 32-byte header, the payload consists of a sequence of cryptographically isolated
nodes. Each node is prefixed by a 7-byte binary descriptor (<HBI: node_id as uint16, node_type
as uint8, plaintext_byte_length as uint32), followed by a 12-byte AES-GCM Initialization Vector
(IV), a 16-byte GCM Authentication Tag, and the encrypted node body.
The UniHeader and the 7-byte node descriptor are passed as Associated Authenticated Data
(AAD) into AES-256-GCM, preventing attackers from splicing or reordering encrypted nodes
across containers.
