4. Cryptographic Notary, \Delta t Timelock, and Duress Steganography
To replace bureaucratic notarization while safeguarding human agency, Node 0
(NOTARY_ANCHOR) implements three cryptographic mechanisms: Two-Phase Cooling-Off Timelock (\Delta t Validation): For high-stakes legal, financial, or medical
consents, cooling_off_delta_t_sec specifies a mandatory time gradient \Delta t > 0 (e.g., 43,200
seconds / 12 hours). Initial signing places the container in
PENDING_DELTA_T_CONFIRMATION. Finalization requires a second cryptographic signature
after T_0 + \Delta t, preventing impulsive decisions made under acute emotional affect (\Delta t
< \text{minutes}).
Dual-Key Duress Steganography (Primary vs. Duress Ed25519 Keys): The user's sovereign key
vault (Zone 0) maintains two distinct Ed25519 keypairs: a Primary Keypair (unlocked via normal
authentication) and a Duress Keypair (unlocked via a coercion PIN/gesture).
If coerced by an attacker, the user signs with the Duress Key.
External Indistinguishability: Standard public signature verification checks math validity against
the signer public key embedded in Node 0 and returns True (VALID). The coercer sees no
warning flags on screen.
Silent Quarantine Routing: When the container reaches the user's personal cloud node or a
trusted syndicate registry that recognizes the Duress Public Key, the node silently routes the
container into Zone 3 (Quarantine) and invalidates execution.
Unidirectional Optical Transport & FEC: For air-gapped hardware (such as the MZM-Pod), the
.uni container is appended with Reed-Solomon RS(255, 223) forward error correction parity
blocks, enabling 100% single-pass recovery over a unidirectional optical data diode without
ACK/NACK feedback channels.
5. Four-Zone Dynamic Memory Triage & Semantic Compression
Host systems managing .uni files segregate storage into four logical and cryptographic memory
zones:
Zone 0 — Sovereign Vault (The Black-Box): Strictly local, offline-capable enclave storing root
keyrings (Primary and Duress seeds), baseline user profile vectors (V_0), and the evolution
audit log (Delta_Audit_Code). Inaccessible to external networks.
Zone 1 — Active Stream: Volatile working memory (RAM/SRAM) protected by ephemeral
session keys (Dead Man's Switch). Upon session timeout or hardware tamper detection (e.g.,
capacitive security mesh trigger), Zone 1 keys are destroyed or SRAM power is shorted to
ground (Crowbar Wipe).
Zone 2 — Semantic Archive (The Graph): Long-term repository of .uni containers.
Background Semantic Merging: During idle/charging states (Asymmetric Triage), the local AI
computes the Cosine Distance between SEMANTIC_TENSOR nodes across Zone 2:
\text{CosineDistance}(\mathbf{A}, \mathbf{B}) = 1 - \frac{\mathbf{A} \cdot
\mathbf{B}}{\Vert{}\mathbf{A}\Vert{} \Vert{}\mathbf{B}\Vert{}}
When \text{CosineDistance} < 0.15, candidate files are merged: duplicate triplets in
KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH are deduplicated, contradictory objects for identical [Subject, Predicate]
pairs are flagged as is_delta_conflict = True (Superposition), and donor file hashes are recorded
in the genealogy tree before archiving originals to cold storage.
Zone 3 — Quarantine (The Honeypot): Isolated sandbox for unverified external files, anomalous
instantaneous ego-shifts (\Delta t < \text{minutes}), and containers signed with a Duress Key.
Purged automatically upon session termination.
